-- M4 fixes round 4 (ctxcat r4 id 3), the NEGATIVE: an axiom must not
-- reach a runtime definition through a zero-constructor family.
-- [Empty] is [Global.Complete []], which [zero_eliminable] accepts, so
-- rounds 1 to 3 stamped [scrut_q = Zero] on this match.  They reached
-- that stamp on the FALLBACK path, i.e. exactly when inference at the
-- ambient mode had already failed, and here it failed with
-- Axiom_runtime_use: the rule that confines an axiom to quantity 0.
-- The fallback forgave it, the match was accepted at quantity Many,
-- and `boom` became a runtime Nat whose erased body is the erasure
-- residue (measured on the round-3 binary: `eval boom` printed
-- <erased>, and `eval (add boom (succ zero))` printed
-- ((add <erased>) (succ zero)), an erasure marker inside a Many
-- computation).  The fallback is now guarded on Erased_use, the ONE
-- class it exists for, so this reports Axiom_runtime_use again.
axiom ff : Empty
def boom : Nat := match ff with end
